1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,530
Podduang,

2
00:00:01,550 --> 00:00:02,920
do you also think

3
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:04,340
that Anda was murdered?

4
00:00:04,530 --> 00:00:06,240
Yeah, I think so, too.

5
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:07,870
Itti,

6
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:09,070
I promise you

7
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:11,240
that if someone is behind this incident,

8
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:13,180
I'll make sure they end up behind bars.

9
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:14,500
Thank you very much, Lieutenant.

10
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:17,610
And you just bought a new one?

11
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:20,480
I bought it online. It didn't cost much.

12
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:23,960
It was probably a QC reject.
The box might be slightly damaged or something.

13
00:00:25,230 --> 00:00:26,370
Dunk, you asshole.

14
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,250
I won't let you borrow my things ever again.

15
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:29,340
Help me.

16
00:00:29,530 --> 00:00:30,680
Help...

17
00:00:30,930 --> 00:00:32,420
Then, would you believe me...

18
00:00:32,439 --> 00:00:33,420
if I told you that...

19
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:35,510
I've heard those voices
for as long as I can remember?

20
00:00:35,540 --> 00:00:36,320
Jin...

21
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:37,230
Jin...

22
00:00:37,250 --> 00:00:37,600
Jin...

23
00:00:37,630 --> 00:00:38,140
Help me.

24
00:00:38,180 --> 00:00:39,100
Hello?

25
00:00:39,350 --> 00:00:40,440
Hello?

26
00:00:40,730 --> 00:00:41,680
Hey, hello?

27
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:42,690
Help me.

28
00:00:42,790 --> 00:00:43,780
Help me.

29
00:00:57,750 --> 00:00:58,970
I'm sorry. Are you okay?

30
00:01:04,209 --> 00:01:05,300
Watch where you're going!

31
00:01:05,330 --> 00:01:07,680
You were too busy on your phone, too.
That's why...

32
00:01:14,270 --> 00:01:16,390
How am I supposed to
get through the day like this?

33
00:01:38,530 --> 00:01:39,870
Does it fit?

34
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:41,910
I didn't know which one to pick.

35
00:01:42,590 --> 00:01:44,900
Well, it does fit,

36
00:01:44,930 --> 00:01:48,180
but I haven't worn a pleated skirt
since I was a freshman.

37
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:49,890
Wearing a long one...

38
00:01:50,250 --> 00:01:51,960
makes me look like a dork.

39
00:01:55,229 --> 00:01:58,190
You look cute in it, though.

40
00:01:59,170 --> 00:02:00,570
Don't you think so?

41
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:05,170
Weren't you embarrassed

42
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:06,860
having to buy a skirt?

43
00:02:06,890 --> 00:02:09,380
If I were, who would have bought it for you?

44
00:02:12,410 --> 00:02:14,710
You're right. So...

45
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:16,700
where are you heading now?

46
00:02:18,030 --> 00:02:21,000
Oh, I'm going to the soccer club.

47
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:23,380
That's perfect. I'll come with you.

48
00:02:25,930 --> 00:02:27,050
Okay.

49
00:02:32,490 --> 00:02:33,610
Put some energy into it.

50
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:34,960
Be more agile.

51
00:02:35,390 --> 00:02:36,670
Don't step on the lines.

52
00:02:37,010 --> 00:02:38,550
Good. Nice.

53
00:02:41,070 --> 00:02:41,950
Go.

54
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:45,570
Keep going.

55
00:03:12,290 --> 00:03:17,110
♫When we happened to hold hands,
was that when it all started?♫

56
00:03:17,130 --> 00:03:21,490
♫When I somehow memorized your number,
was that when you took my heart?♫

57
00:03:21,490 --> 00:03:23,970
What are you doing? Are you going to sit down?

58
00:03:34,690 --> 00:03:35,950
So,

59
00:03:36,640 --> 00:03:38,260
is Jin really flirting with you?

60
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:42,140
Well, something like that.

61
00:03:43,290 --> 00:03:44,350
How is that possible?

62
00:03:44,930 --> 00:03:46,090
You're...

63
00:03:48,210 --> 00:03:50,079
not even his type.

64
00:03:52,390 --> 00:03:55,280
By the way, do you like him?

65
00:03:59,610 --> 00:04:00,990
Why do you ask?

66
00:04:01,010 --> 00:04:04,570
Well, I just want to know. Do you like him?

67
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:12,520
I don't know. We've only just started talking.

68
00:04:25,610 --> 00:04:27,280
Then I'm gonna go for Jin.

69
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:35,000
Suit yourself.

70
00:04:53,450 --> 00:04:55,850
[The depicted characters, behaviors, locations,
organizations, professions, and events]

71
00:04:55,880 --> 00:04:57,370
[are fictional and created
for entertainment purposes only.]

72
00:04:57,390 --> 00:04:59,430
[It is not intended to endorse or promote
any of the actions or behavior depicted.]

73
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:00,720
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

74
00:05:13,220 --> 00:05:18,880
♫I used to wonder what we were,♫

75
00:05:19,700 --> 00:05:25,530
♫I thought love needed something clearer,♫

76
00:05:26,370 --> 00:05:31,620
♫Took me time to learn what really matters♫

77
00:05:33,220 --> 00:05:38,300
♫Love has no rules, whatever comes after♫

78
00:05:39,700 --> 00:05:45,090
♫As long as I know what my heart wants to find,♫

79
00:05:45,490 --> 00:05:48,010
♫As long as you're standing by my side,♫

80
00:05:48,050 --> 00:05:51,340
♫With you, the only one I'd choose every time,♫

81
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:55,200
♫I don't need a reason, as long as you're mine♫

82
00:05:55,760 --> 00:05:58,150
♫As long as you hold my hand,♫

83
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:01,370
♫As long as next to me is where you stand,♫

84
00:06:01,370 --> 00:06:04,730
♫You're the one I'll always try to understand,♫

85
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:08,560
♫No matter how hard the road may be,♫

86
00:06:09,020 --> 00:06:11,500
♫Just hold my hand, and we'll be free♫

87
00:06:12,370 --> 00:06:15,010
♫As long as you're here with me♫

88
00:06:20,110 --> 00:06:21,860
He's the one who killed Anda.

89
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:24,750
Just confess already.

90
00:06:25,450 --> 00:06:26,800
- Tell everyone you killed him!
- Stop it.

91
00:06:26,830 --> 00:06:27,790
That's enough.

92
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:29,270
This is going too far.

93
00:06:29,990 --> 00:06:31,350
My parents are sitting right there.

94
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:33,850
At the very least, show them some respect.

95
00:06:39,520 --> 00:06:40,840
Do you really think...

96
00:06:41,590 --> 00:06:43,409
that Anda killed himself?

97
00:06:45,230 --> 00:06:46,960
What I think is none of your business.

98
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:48,780
As for a partner like you,

99
00:06:49,490 --> 00:06:52,250
who only cares about losing your job
now that my brother is dead,

100
00:06:52,740 --> 00:06:54,500
go throw your tantrum somewhere else.

101
00:06:54,530 --> 00:06:56,450
Don't do it at my brother's funeral.

102
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:58,159
You...

103
00:06:59,630 --> 00:07:00,970
ruined my life.

104
00:07:00,990 --> 00:07:01,870
You bastard!

105
00:07:01,870 --> 00:07:02,690
Go.

106
00:07:03,740 --> 00:07:04,470
Leave.

107
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:16,200
As for you,

108
00:07:17,610 --> 00:07:20,090
I don't see any need for you to be here.

109
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:25,730
Kum was Anda's boyfriend, after all.

110
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:29,240
I don't think it's unusual for him
to be at his funeral.

111
00:07:30,050 --> 00:07:33,280
That's right.
I think he has every reason to be here.

112
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:46,370
Come on, Mom.

113
00:07:50,070 --> 00:07:51,040
Are you okay?

114
00:07:51,780 --> 00:07:52,650
I am.

115
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:54,720
Thanks.

116
00:08:08,190 --> 00:08:11,260
I know you're sad,
but you should eat something.

117
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:13,650
Here, it's still warm.

118
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,940
Yeah, you need to eat.

119
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:21,860
You've lost so much weight.

120
00:08:27,290 --> 00:08:31,530
You know what makes you look suspicious?
The way you're acting right now.

121
00:08:32,500 --> 00:08:36,440
I know you're grieving and can't process it yet,

122
00:08:36,789 --> 00:08:39,400
but you have to prove your innocence, too.

123
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:45,030
Sorry, can I ask you something?

124
00:08:46,780 --> 00:08:48,350
Why did you say

125
00:08:49,180 --> 00:08:50,960
you were the reason Anda died?

126
00:08:51,290 --> 00:08:56,170
I know you didn't mean you killed him,

127
00:08:56,190 --> 00:08:58,790
but I want to know

128
00:08:59,990 --> 00:09:04,470
if it has anything to do
with you breaking up with him?

129
00:09:05,130 --> 00:09:05,740
You're...

130
00:09:05,770 --> 00:09:08,670
Oh, I'm Podduang.

131
00:09:08,970 --> 00:09:12,210
Let's just say I'm a friend of Anda's friend.

132
00:09:18,770 --> 00:09:19,800
It does.

133
00:09:21,810 --> 00:09:23,650
That breakup message...

134
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,090
was actually from me.

135
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:32,610
But if I'd known that
he was facing something much worse than that,

136
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:36,480
the pressure I was under...

137
00:09:37,560 --> 00:09:39,150
would have meant nothing.

138
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:46,280
Who was putting pressure on you?

139
00:09:50,680 --> 00:09:51,920
Well...

140
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:54,680
That day...

141
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:57,020
Can't you answer that?

142
00:09:58,120 --> 00:09:59,520
I asked...

143
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:03,440
how much longer you planned to stay together.

144
00:10:11,130 --> 00:10:12,030
No answer?

145
00:10:12,750 --> 00:10:14,170
Then I guess

146
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:18,720
that means you can't see it either, right?

147
00:10:19,030 --> 00:10:21,770
You can't see how long the love between two men

148
00:10:22,660 --> 00:10:24,700
can really last.

149
00:10:33,770 --> 00:10:34,710
Sir,

150
00:10:35,520 --> 00:10:36,380
well...

151
00:10:38,100 --> 00:10:41,300
I know it might seem strange to you,

152
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:45,030
but I intend to love

153
00:10:46,730 --> 00:10:48,570
and take care of Anda forever,

154
00:10:50,210 --> 00:10:51,770
or for as long as possible.

155
00:10:52,910 --> 00:10:55,120
Just like any other couple.

156
00:10:55,890 --> 00:10:57,460
Aren't you ashamed of what people think?

157
00:10:57,760 --> 00:10:59,410
Two men living together?

158
00:11:04,280 --> 00:11:05,080
I...

159
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:08,520
I'm not ashamed.

160
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:13,680
Do you think...

161
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:16,420
Anda will be ashamed, though?

162
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:22,170
My son is still young.

163
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,440
He's still naive.

164
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:30,500
What if one day he comes to his senses

165
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:33,700
and looks back on this, only to realize...

166
00:11:33,730 --> 00:11:35,620
he was wrong to do this?

167
00:11:35,650 --> 00:11:36,930
Won't he be ashamed?

168
00:11:38,650 --> 00:11:39,460
Look.

169
00:11:40,410 --> 00:11:42,160
Anda is famous.

170
00:11:42,540 --> 00:11:44,780
His family comes
from an old, refined background.

171
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:48,200
He's not just anybody

172
00:11:48,220 --> 00:11:50,210
who can do whatever he wants.

173
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:51,360
Do you realize that?

174
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:07,480
I'm begging you.

175
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:12,080
Can you let him go for now?

176
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:21,520
At the very least,

177
00:12:23,340 --> 00:12:25,140
let him grow up first.

178
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:27,500
Let him become more mature,

179
00:12:30,810 --> 00:12:33,080
learn more about the world,

180
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:40,840
and experience the adult world for himself
before he makes up his mind.

181
00:12:44,810 --> 00:12:46,130
And when that day comes,

182
00:12:47,140 --> 00:12:50,100
if he still insists on being with you,

183
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:53,350
I will give it another thought.

184
00:12:57,770 --> 00:12:58,760
However,

185
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:01,520
for now,

186
00:13:04,550 --> 00:13:06,460
I'm asking you to help Anda.

187
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:11,560
It hurts both me and my wife

188
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:14,180
every time we see our own son

189
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:17,240
being attacked by people online.

190
00:13:20,580 --> 00:13:22,580
I raised him well.

191
00:13:35,050 --> 00:13:36,800
Don't ruin his life.

192
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:14,080
So...

193
00:14:16,370 --> 00:14:19,160
you texted Anda to break up with him?

194
00:14:22,810 --> 00:14:23,730
Yes.

195
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:28,340
Right then and there.

196
00:14:29,180 --> 00:14:30,460
I let his dad see it.

197
00:14:32,970 --> 00:14:33,970
That means...

198
00:14:35,050 --> 00:14:36,900
you were at Anda's house the whole time?

199
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:37,960
That's right.

200
00:14:38,730 --> 00:14:40,930
I told you I didn't kill him.

201
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:45,010
How could I hurt the person I love most?

202
00:14:49,740 --> 00:14:50,520
Then...

203
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:53,160
who do you think killed him?

204
00:14:54,050 --> 00:14:55,590
I'll be honest with you, Jin.

205
00:14:58,570 --> 00:15:01,730
If you ever went through something like this...

206
00:15:04,170 --> 00:15:07,840
If the person you loved most
was suddenly taken from you,

207
00:15:11,390 --> 00:15:13,070
you wouldn't care about anything.

208
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:17,890
The culprit, the cause of death,
or anything else.

209
00:15:19,320 --> 00:15:20,960
All you'd think about

210
00:15:23,090 --> 00:15:25,000
is a life without them.

211
00:15:25,990 --> 00:15:27,600
You'd just feel like...

212
00:15:28,200 --> 00:15:31,240
your world had already fallen apart.

213
00:15:33,290 --> 00:15:34,810
Who the culprit is,

214
00:15:35,470 --> 00:15:36,870
or who did it,

215
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:40,400
I don't know.

216
00:15:43,900 --> 00:15:45,310
I'm sorry.

217
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:48,680
I was so focused on finding the culprit

218
00:15:48,930 --> 00:15:50,570
that I didn't think about
what you were going through.

219
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:56,120
It's okay.

220
00:15:56,650 --> 00:15:57,670
I understand.

221
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:01,740
Anyway, I have to thank you all

222
00:16:02,530 --> 00:16:04,570
for trying so hard for Anda.

223
00:16:08,680 --> 00:16:12,560
If there's anything I can do to help,
just let me know.

224
00:16:12,910 --> 00:16:14,750
I'm more than happy to do my best.

225
00:16:16,650 --> 00:16:17,930
I also want to know

226
00:16:19,820 --> 00:16:23,230
who was cruel enough to do this to Anda.

227
00:16:31,850 --> 00:16:34,540
Alright, let's eat.

228
00:16:34,570 --> 00:16:35,810
Let's stop stressing out.

229
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:37,040
Come on.

230
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:40,490
Come on, have some food.

231
00:16:42,970 --> 00:16:44,210
Do you want anything?

232
00:16:44,710 --> 00:16:46,440
This is fine. The rice porridge.

233
00:16:48,710 --> 00:16:49,760
Go ahead.

234
00:17:06,130 --> 00:17:08,650
It wasn't Itti,
the last person to be with him.

235
00:17:11,569 --> 00:17:14,420
And it wasn't Kum,
the one who broke up with him.

236
00:17:18,530 --> 00:17:20,210
Then who did this to you, Anda?

237
00:17:20,730 --> 00:17:21,760
Who was it?

238
00:17:46,450 --> 00:17:47,790
What the hell are you looking at?

239
00:17:47,810 --> 00:17:50,410
Oh, you're still doing okay?

240
00:17:50,930 --> 00:17:52,840
I heard you screaming in your room last night.

241
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:55,540
I'm fine.

242
00:17:56,210 --> 00:17:57,660
Where are you going?

243
00:17:59,260 --> 00:18:00,340
I'm going swimming.

244
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:02,890
Wanna come? It might help relieve your stress.

245
00:18:04,090 --> 00:18:06,440
Or just stay in your room
and keep screaming into your pillow.

246
00:18:07,690 --> 00:18:08,650
Fine.

247
00:18:16,330 --> 00:18:19,250
What's gotten into you,
going swimming at this hour?

248
00:18:19,610 --> 00:18:22,780
This is the best time
to get the adrenaline pumping

249
00:18:23,170 --> 00:18:24,510
so I can stay active all day.

250
00:18:25,950 --> 00:18:28,610
Your life must be nice.
You don't have anything to worry about.

251
00:18:33,900 --> 00:18:34,860
Podduang!

252
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:52,920
Podduang!

253
00:19:41,530 --> 00:19:42,730
What are you looking at?

254
00:19:45,260 --> 00:19:46,710
You're in really good shape.

255
00:19:48,670 --> 00:19:49,880
Well, I'm an athlete.

256
00:19:50,530 --> 00:19:51,570
How could I not be in shape?

257
00:19:52,890 --> 00:19:54,830
You should exercise more yourself

258
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:56,440
since you're just that tiny.

259
00:19:59,050 --> 00:20:01,960
I'm what they call compact.

260
00:20:06,730 --> 00:20:09,570
Are you really a swimming instructor?

261
00:20:11,160 --> 00:20:14,200
Yeah, why would I lie?

262
00:20:15,790 --> 00:20:18,430
I teach elementary kids.
Just private lessons.

263
00:20:19,050 --> 00:20:20,590
So I have to come here to teach them.

264
00:20:21,090 --> 00:20:22,720
They live in the same place you do.

265
00:20:26,380 --> 00:20:27,740
You sure do so many things.

266
00:20:47,540 --> 00:20:48,680
What are you thinking about?

267
00:20:51,820 --> 00:20:53,100
About Anda.

268
00:20:56,220 --> 00:20:58,100
I don't know how to help him.

269
00:21:00,340 --> 00:21:01,740
The police are so slow.

270
00:21:02,140 --> 00:21:03,140
They're useless.

271
00:21:05,580 --> 00:21:06,840
Did you bring your earbuds?

272
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:17,430
I tried to listen this morning,
but I couldn't hear anything.

273
00:21:25,120 --> 00:21:27,200
Can I keep them for now?

274
00:21:28,100 --> 00:21:29,140
What for?

275
00:21:30,140 --> 00:21:34,980
Didn't you say you didn't hear anything?

276
00:21:36,010 --> 00:21:37,520
So why keep them?

277
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:39,380
You can use mine for now.

278
00:21:40,140 --> 00:21:42,900
Man, just take them, then.

279
00:21:44,060 --> 00:21:45,340
I'll just buy new ones.

280
00:21:46,450 --> 00:21:48,230
I don't like using things
someone else has used before.

281
00:21:49,620 --> 00:21:50,920
So I'm someone else now?

282
00:21:52,970 --> 00:21:54,390
Yeah, just take them.

283
00:21:54,420 --> 00:21:55,900
I'll find something for myself.

284
00:22:05,280 --> 00:22:08,720
But I got these earbuds from Dunk.

285
00:22:13,340 --> 00:22:15,060
Where did he buy them?

286
00:22:24,820 --> 00:22:27,910
You called me over just to ask
where I bought these earbuds?

287
00:22:27,940 --> 00:22:30,060
Why didn't you just call? I'm busy.

288
00:22:30,580 --> 00:22:33,740
Busy with what? You were playing games loudly,
trying to make my ears bleed.

289
00:22:36,160 --> 00:22:37,000
Dunk,

290
00:22:38,360 --> 00:22:40,190
where did you get these earbuds?

291
00:22:40,220 --> 00:22:42,390
I bought them from an online shop.

292
00:22:42,420 --> 00:22:43,590
My regular page.

293
00:22:43,610 --> 00:22:45,710
They sell literally everything.

294
00:22:45,740 --> 00:22:47,540
Which page? Let me see.

295
00:22:49,060 --> 00:22:49,890
Is it this one?

296
00:22:50,470 --> 00:22:52,080
We've got stuff from everywhere today.

297
00:22:52,110 --> 00:22:53,350
We have everything.

298
00:22:53,370 --> 00:22:55,200
Everything you'd ever want, guys.

299
00:22:55,220 --> 00:22:57,030
Yeah, they're live right now.

300
00:22:58,740 --> 00:22:59,710
I knew it.

301
00:22:59,730 --> 00:23:02,960
This page... They either sell fakes
or knock-offs.

302
00:23:02,980 --> 00:23:05,120
Wait, they told me they were QC rejects.

303
00:23:06,080 --> 00:23:07,240
Let me see.

304
00:23:09,420 --> 00:23:12,800
Various shirts in various styles.

305
00:23:12,820 --> 00:23:15,610
What should be our special item today?

306
00:23:15,630 --> 00:23:16,840
We've got jackets today.

307
00:23:19,150 --> 00:23:20,090
Cool?

308
00:23:20,460 --> 00:23:22,220
- Is something wrong?
- So many of them.

309
00:23:22,940 --> 00:23:25,070
- The jacket the vendor is wearing...
- They're all high quality.

310
00:23:25,660 --> 00:23:26,620
Why?

311
00:23:28,340 --> 00:23:29,220
I bought this jacket...

312
00:23:30,340 --> 00:23:31,880
for Anda.

313
00:23:38,360 --> 00:23:40,120
I'm sure it's the same one.

314
00:23:42,760 --> 00:23:43,900
Got it. Boots.

315
00:23:43,900 --> 00:23:44,850
Got it.

316
00:23:44,870 --> 00:23:46,460
You're getting them, too, right?

317
00:23:53,560 --> 00:23:54,880
Are you serious?

318
00:23:54,900 --> 00:23:58,100
I have no idea where they get their stock.

319
00:23:58,400 --> 00:23:59,870
Do you think they'll tell you

320
00:23:59,890 --> 00:24:01,530
where they got the earbuds?

321
00:24:02,450 --> 00:24:03,810
They'll have to.

322
00:24:07,800 --> 00:24:09,000
Oh, Art?

323
00:24:09,020 --> 00:24:10,340
Hello, Art.

324
00:24:10,370 --> 00:24:12,690
Whoa, a regular customer!

325
00:24:12,710 --> 00:24:14,920
You're picking up the shirt yourself today, huh?

326
00:24:15,730 --> 00:24:16,840
Are you in a hurry to use it?

327
00:24:16,860 --> 00:24:17,670
Yes.

328
00:24:17,690 --> 00:24:21,230
By the way, there's another one
I actually want.

329
00:24:21,250 --> 00:24:24,220
I saw you wearing it
in the livestream. This one.

330
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:28,320
Oh, right.
I was just wearing it in the livestream.

331
00:24:28,620 --> 00:24:29,800
Cute, isn't it?

332
00:24:29,820 --> 00:24:32,220
But it belongs to my friend.
It's not for sale.

333
00:24:32,260 --> 00:24:35,520
Why? Why is it not for sale?

334
00:24:35,540 --> 00:24:36,970
How much do you want?

335
00:24:37,660 --> 00:24:39,350
It's not about the price.

336
00:24:39,370 --> 00:24:40,590
It's just not mine to sell.

337
00:24:40,620 --> 00:24:42,110
There are plenty of other clothes.

338
00:24:42,130 --> 00:24:43,890
Lots of cool items. Take your pick.

339
00:24:46,280 --> 00:24:47,690
It really is Anda's.

340
00:24:47,710 --> 00:24:49,380
I had this embroidered here.

341
00:24:50,740 --> 00:24:52,740
This one really isn't for sale.

342
00:24:56,070 --> 00:24:57,860
Take me to your friend.

343
00:24:58,180 --> 00:25:00,350
Please calm down. Calm down, okay?

344
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:02,060
Li.

345
00:25:02,580 --> 00:25:04,410
What is it now?

346
00:25:04,940 --> 00:25:07,360
Oh, you're bringing me a guy?

347
00:25:07,820 --> 00:25:09,620
Yeah, they're here to see you.

348
00:25:11,200 --> 00:25:12,720
Where did you get this jacket?

349
00:25:15,740 --> 00:25:18,230
I don't remember.

350
00:25:18,250 --> 00:25:19,880
I don't know. I can't remember.

351
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:22,840
I asked where you got this jacket.

352
00:25:25,680 --> 00:25:27,470
Maybe it's my dad's.

353
00:25:27,490 --> 00:25:29,040
I don't know where he bought it.

354
00:25:29,060 --> 00:25:30,780
I thought it looked nice,
so I just grabbed it.

355
00:25:30,810 --> 00:25:32,330
Call your dad

356
00:25:33,140 --> 00:25:34,680
and ask him where he got this jacket.

357
00:25:42,960 --> 00:25:44,000
Hello?

358
00:25:44,660 --> 00:25:46,270
Hello, Dad.

359
00:25:46,300 --> 00:25:49,350
Where did you get this new jacket?

360
00:25:50,250 --> 00:25:51,280
Which one?

361
00:25:51,540 --> 00:25:54,430
The denim jacket with the leather collar.

362
00:25:54,960 --> 00:25:56,300
Oh...

363
00:25:57,690 --> 00:26:01,160
I got it somewhere near where I work.

364
00:26:01,330 --> 00:26:03,610
Are you sure you didn't take it from anyone?

365
00:26:04,240 --> 00:26:06,030
Yeah, why are you asking?

366
00:26:06,050 --> 00:26:08,480
I wouldn't steal from anyone. That's it.

367
00:26:08,510 --> 00:26:10,590
Okay, talk to you later.

368
00:26:13,230 --> 00:26:15,220
Take me to your dad.

369
00:26:31,070 --> 00:26:32,280
Well...

370
00:26:32,310 --> 00:26:33,610
​Who are these people?

371
00:26:33,630 --> 00:26:35,190
​Where did you get this jacket?

372
00:26:39,250 --> 00:26:40,930
​Why do you want to know?

373
00:26:40,950 --> 00:26:42,430
​I won't beat around the bush.

374
00:26:43,110 --> 00:26:44,870
This is my friend's jacket,

375
00:26:45,550 --> 00:26:47,540
but he just died a few days ago.

376
00:26:48,830 --> 00:26:49,970
​I want to know

377
00:26:50,750 --> 00:26:52,430
​how his jacket ended up with you.

378
00:26:58,800 --> 00:27:01,360
​Well, I took it from...

379
00:27:01,390 --> 00:27:02,940
From the dead man's car, right?

380
00:27:04,830 --> 00:27:05,990
​Just answer me.

381
00:27:09,410 --> 00:27:10,850
​Dad, just tell them

382
00:27:10,880 --> 00:27:12,350
where you got this jacket.

383
00:27:12,370 --> 00:27:14,030
​They won't report you to the police.

384
00:27:14,050 --> 00:27:15,990
​You really won't report him, right?

385
00:27:20,270 --> 00:27:23,040
​If you tell me everything, I won't report you.

386
00:27:23,950 --> 00:27:26,910
You do know
theft can get you sent to prison, right?

387
00:27:34,030 --> 00:27:35,570
​I didn't know he was dead.

388
00:27:35,600 --> 00:27:37,790
​I thought he was just sleeping.

389
00:27:44,980 --> 00:27:46,020
​So...

390
00:27:47,750 --> 00:27:49,540
​you really did go to that car.

391
00:27:51,230 --> 00:27:55,380
​Dammit, a security guard's salary
isn't enough to live on.

392
00:27:55,410 --> 00:27:58,010
​I just do some petty thievery here and there.

393
00:27:59,630 --> 00:28:01,340
I really need the money.

394
00:28:02,450 --> 00:28:04,140
​And I'm not hurting anyone.

395
00:28:04,160 --> 00:28:05,700
I just steal stuff,

396
00:28:06,140 --> 00:28:07,620
and it's not like I do it every day.

397
00:28:07,650 --> 00:28:09,430
​You don't have to make other excuses.

398
00:28:10,710 --> 00:28:12,100
​I want to know about this.

399
00:28:13,290 --> 00:28:15,170
​What did you see when you went to that car?

400
00:28:15,170 --> 00:28:16,600
​Tell me everything.

401
00:28:19,330 --> 00:28:22,170
​Well, I saw a car
that had been parked there for a while.

402
00:28:25,050 --> 00:28:25,750
​Hey.

403
00:28:25,770 --> 00:28:28,540
​So I tried opening the door,
hoping it wasn't locked.

404
00:28:29,810 --> 00:28:33,010
But when it opened, I was shocked
to see someone sleeping inside.

405
00:28:33,370 --> 00:28:35,410
​Was he dead at that time?

406
00:28:36,050 --> 00:28:39,730
​Whoa, I wouldn't know.
I just knew he was sleeping.

407
00:28:39,980 --> 00:28:42,220
So I just grabbed some valuables

408
00:28:42,240 --> 00:28:43,900
and got out of there.

409
00:28:43,930 --> 00:28:45,400
​What did you take?

410
00:28:49,010 --> 00:28:51,490
The cash in the bag

411
00:28:51,490 --> 00:28:54,130
and this jacket.

412
00:28:54,590 --> 00:28:57,270
What about the phone and the laptop?
Did you take them?

413
00:28:59,770 --> 00:29:03,490
Yeah. The phone and the laptop, too.

414
00:29:07,720 --> 00:29:08,860
Where are they now?

415
00:29:10,860 --> 00:29:12,570
I've already sold them.

416
00:29:18,070 --> 00:29:20,500
​Why were you in such a hurry to sell them?

417
00:29:20,530 --> 00:29:22,430
Come on, they were stolen.

418
00:29:22,450 --> 00:29:24,850
I had to get rid of them as fast as possible.

419
00:29:25,530 --> 00:29:29,610
My daughter took this jacket with her,
so it's the only thing left.

420
00:29:29,870 --> 00:29:31,700
​As for the rest, I've sold them all.

421
00:29:32,690 --> 00:29:36,430
​The phone and laptop are probably
at the border by now.

422
00:29:37,200 --> 00:29:38,730
​You won't be able to track them down.

423
00:29:49,090 --> 00:29:53,530
Dad, who did you sell
the dead man's phone and laptop to?

424
00:29:54,950 --> 00:29:56,990
Maybe they can buy them back.

425
00:29:57,020 --> 00:29:58,930
​It seems they're looking for something.

426
00:30:04,050 --> 00:30:05,390
​I can't tell you.

427
00:30:06,210 --> 00:30:07,430
​Those things...

428
00:30:07,450 --> 00:30:10,370
are with someone
we should stay far away from.

429
00:30:31,680 --> 00:30:33,880
​Why does everyone always try to startle me?

430
00:30:35,370 --> 00:30:37,040
​You're such a scaredy-cat.

431
00:30:38,010 --> 00:30:39,210
​What were you thinking about?

432
00:30:42,220 --> 00:30:46,450
How are we going to find
Anda's phone and laptop?

433
00:30:48,040 --> 00:30:49,670
​There might be a way.

434
00:30:49,700 --> 00:30:51,280
Let me think about it first.

435
00:30:51,300 --> 00:30:52,840
​I'm so exhausted right now.

436
00:31:02,160 --> 00:31:03,140
Eat up.

437
00:31:03,450 --> 00:31:04,530
This one is good.

438
00:31:07,630 --> 00:31:08,450
Eat, come on.

439
00:31:08,860 --> 00:31:11,200
Yeah, I'm literally chewing.

440
00:31:15,150 --> 00:31:16,550
Have some more.

441
00:31:17,960 --> 00:31:19,070
By the way,

442
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:22,020
what's the occasion for this treat?

443
00:31:23,370 --> 00:31:24,570
Nothing, really.

444
00:31:25,530 --> 00:31:27,410
We've been going through a lot lately,

445
00:31:28,170 --> 00:31:31,690
so I thought we could enjoy some food
and take a break from all the stress.

446
00:31:42,660 --> 00:31:43,620
What?

447
00:31:45,250 --> 00:31:47,330
Do I look like someone
who only talks about depressing stuff?

448
00:31:48,330 --> 00:31:50,250
Exactly. You just realized?

449
00:31:52,040 --> 00:31:53,160
You look...

450
00:31:53,970 --> 00:31:55,490
so unwelcoming.

451
00:31:56,440 --> 00:31:58,910
That's why I've hated your guts all this time.

452
00:32:03,960 --> 00:32:05,240
Be careful.

453
00:32:05,790 --> 00:32:08,330
You might end up with what you hate.

454
00:32:15,860 --> 00:32:18,180
Sir, please buy some cupcakes.

455
00:32:20,080 --> 00:32:23,160
Do you know what time it is?
You should go home.

456
00:32:23,780 --> 00:32:26,850
I haven't sold them all yet,
so I can't go home.

457
00:32:29,640 --> 00:32:31,680
Did your parents make you do this?

458
00:32:32,950 --> 00:32:35,080
Jin, don't be so harsh on him.

459
00:32:37,940 --> 00:32:40,700
No, sir. My dad is sick and can barely walk.

460
00:32:40,720 --> 00:32:42,630
My mom passed away a long time ago.

461
00:32:48,730 --> 00:32:50,280
Who do you live with?

462
00:32:51,150 --> 00:32:53,110
With my dad and my younger sister.

463
00:32:53,140 --> 00:32:56,580
My dad makes these cupcakes.
My mom taught him the recipe.

464
00:33:01,200 --> 00:33:02,420
Have you eaten yet?

465
00:33:02,800 --> 00:33:03,980
Not yet, sir.

466
00:33:07,970 --> 00:33:09,930
Have something first,
then I'll buy your cupcakes.

467
00:33:10,770 --> 00:33:13,630
I can't stay long, sir.
I need to sell all the cupcakes.

468
00:33:15,220 --> 00:33:18,050
I'll buy them all, but you should eat first.

469
00:33:22,850 --> 00:33:24,530
Eat with us.

470
00:33:25,230 --> 00:33:26,710
You'll be home in no time.

471
00:33:28,490 --> 00:33:30,420
My friend eats a lot.

472
00:33:30,440 --> 00:33:32,600
He'll buy up all your cupcakes himself.

473
00:33:34,450 --> 00:33:35,450
Would it be okay

474
00:33:35,480 --> 00:33:38,710
if I wrapped up the food you gave me
and took it home instead?

475
00:33:39,520 --> 00:33:41,650
Hey, just eat it here.

476
00:33:41,680 --> 00:33:43,120
Why do you want to take it home?

477
00:33:44,640 --> 00:33:47,060
I want to take it for my dad and sister.

478
00:33:59,240 --> 00:34:00,400
Sir,

479
00:34:00,910 --> 00:34:04,430
I want one set
of everything on this table to go.

480
00:34:09,540 --> 00:34:10,780
Are you happy now?

481
00:34:12,929 --> 00:34:14,409
Can you eat with us now?

482
00:34:15,739 --> 00:34:17,110
Thank you, handsome.

483
00:34:17,139 --> 00:34:19,540
I hope only good things come your way.

484
00:34:21,949 --> 00:34:23,260
Aw, "handsome."

485
00:34:25,409 --> 00:34:26,179
Come here.

486
00:34:31,630 --> 00:34:32,949
Here you go.

487
00:34:34,020 --> 00:34:35,980
Can you eat this? Let me do it for you.

488
00:34:36,540 --> 00:34:37,520
How much of this do you want?

489
00:34:55,340 --> 00:34:56,940
Get him a glass.

490
00:34:58,860 --> 00:35:00,620
I forgot. My bad.

491
00:35:27,980 --> 00:35:29,210
Hey, Jin.

492
00:35:29,640 --> 00:35:33,030
Why did you have to help that kid so much?

493
00:35:33,060 --> 00:35:36,120
Couldn't you just buy some of his cupcakes
and leave it at that?

494
00:35:38,070 --> 00:35:39,650
I used to have nothing.

495
00:35:39,930 --> 00:35:41,710
He reminds me of myself.

496
00:35:42,180 --> 00:35:43,310
Why?

497
00:35:43,590 --> 00:35:46,630
Is it that questionable
when I do something good?

498
00:35:46,660 --> 00:35:48,430
Hey, I was just asking.

499
00:35:48,450 --> 00:35:49,840
Why so prickly?

500
00:35:51,020 --> 00:35:52,660
I was actually complimenting you.

501
00:35:55,100 --> 00:35:56,580
No need for that.

502
00:35:57,860 --> 00:35:59,700
You deserve a reward
when you do something good.

503
00:36:00,670 --> 00:36:01,990
Do you want anything?

504
00:36:02,010 --> 00:36:03,220
I'll get it for you.

505
00:36:03,950 --> 00:36:05,310
I can buy it myself.

506
00:36:05,340 --> 00:36:06,420
No need to get me anything.

507
00:36:06,740 --> 00:36:08,780
There's nothing I want right now.

508
00:36:09,640 --> 00:36:11,280
I'm sure there's something

509
00:36:11,310 --> 00:36:12,670
that you really want,

510
00:36:13,930 --> 00:36:15,570
but money can't buy.

511
00:36:29,200 --> 00:36:30,110
Hurry.

512
00:36:52,830 --> 00:36:55,860
Hey, I'm soaked. It's all over me.

513
00:36:56,780 --> 00:36:58,520
You look like a drowned rat.

514
00:37:00,740 --> 00:37:03,570
So, what were you going to give me just now?

515
00:37:07,330 --> 00:37:08,350
You're not getting it.

516
00:37:08,900 --> 00:37:10,420
You said you didn't want it.

517
00:37:12,500 --> 00:37:13,300
So,

518
00:37:13,900 --> 00:37:15,420
you're really not giving it to me?

519
00:37:25,790 --> 00:37:27,350
Actually, there is something...

520
00:37:27,890 --> 00:37:29,830
I want but haven't gotten yet.

521
00:37:33,650 --> 00:37:34,610
And...

522
00:37:35,440 --> 00:37:36,760
do you still want it?

523
00:37:38,950 --> 00:37:40,060
I do.

524
00:37:45,460 --> 00:37:50,300
Do you know which bus lines
go past my condo?

525
00:37:55,330 --> 00:37:57,780
Line 084.

526
00:38:03,290 --> 00:38:05,390
Line 156.

527
00:38:07,020 --> 00:38:09,100
Are you sure those are bus lines?

528
00:38:12,780 --> 00:38:14,180
Line 44.

529
00:38:16,830 --> 00:38:19,030
- Hold on.
- And then 65.

530
00:38:24,900 --> 00:38:28,020
084... 156, right?

531
00:38:31,360 --> 00:38:33,000
084156...

532
00:38:33,340 --> 00:38:34,650
What was it again?

533
00:38:35,660 --> 00:38:37,120
44, right?

534
00:38:37,740 --> 00:38:38,900
44 and...

535
00:38:40,990 --> 00:38:42,410
5 and what?

536
00:38:43,390 --> 00:38:46,270
- 5...
- Jeez, you don't remember?

537
00:38:52,970 --> 00:38:54,660
65...

538
00:38:56,300 --> 00:38:57,630
Not 56.

539
00:39:00,590 --> 00:39:04,310
So, can I call you?

540
00:39:05,190 --> 00:39:07,200
Don't you call me all the time anyway?

541
00:39:07,650 --> 00:39:11,060
Come on, calling the number is way more classic.

542
00:39:16,740 --> 00:39:18,200
Do whatever you want.

543
00:39:25,880 --> 00:39:27,800
So I can do whatever I want?

544
00:39:30,700 --> 00:39:31,660
Yeah.

545
00:39:34,300 --> 00:39:36,590
Have I ever tried to stop you?

546
00:39:41,510 --> 00:39:46,610
♫When we happened to hold hands,
was that when it all started?♫

547
00:39:46,630 --> 00:39:51,390
